# 4️⃣ Validate Binary Search Tree

## 📖 Problem

Determine whether a Binary Tree is a valid BST.

Example:

```text
        5
       / \
      3   7
```

Valid BST:

```text
true
```

But:

```text
        5
       / \
      3   4
```

is also locally ordered at the root, but depending on the full structure, validity must be checked against the allowed range of each node.

Example of an invalid tree:

```text
        5
       / \
      3   7
         /
        4
```

This is valid.

But:

```text
        5
       / \
      3   7
         /
        2
```

is invalid because `2` belongs to the right subtree of `5` but is smaller than `5`.

---

# 5️⃣ Range-Based Validation

For every node, maintain:

```text
Minimum Allowed Value

Maximum Allowed Value
```

Initially:

```text
(-∞, +∞)
```

For the left child:

```text
(min, root->data)
```

For the right child:

```text
(root->data, max)
```

---

### C++ Code

```cpp
bool validate(
    Node* root,
    long long minValue,
    long long maxValue)
{
    if(root == NULL)
        return true;

    if(root->data <= minValue ||
       root->data >= maxValue)
        return false;

    return validate(
        root->left,
        minValue,
        root->data
    )
    &&
    validate(
        root->right,
        root->data,
        maxValue
    );
}

bool isValidBST(Node* root)
{
    return validate(
        root,
        LLONG_MIN,
        LLONG_MAX
    );
}
```

### Complexity

```text
Time: O(n)

Space: O(h)
```

