# 6️⃣ Lowest Common Ancestor in BST

## 📖 Problem

Find the Lowest Common Ancestor of two nodes in a BST.

Example:

```text
          6
        /   \
       2     8
      / \   / \
     0   4 7   9
        / \
       3   5
```

For:

```text
2 and 8
```

LCA:

```text
6
```

For:

```text
2 and 4
```

LCA:

```text
2
```

---

# 7️⃣ LCA Using BST Property

At every node:

### If both values are smaller:

```text
p < root
q < root
```

Move:

```text
LEFT
```

### If both values are greater:

```text
p > root
q > root
```

Move:

```text
RIGHT
```

### Otherwise:

The current node is the LCA.

---

### C++ Code

```cpp
Node* lowestCommonAncestor(
    Node* root,
    Node* p,
    Node* q)
{
    while(root != NULL)
    {
        if(p->data < root->data &&
           q->data < root->data)
        {
            root = root->left;
        }
        else if(p->data > root->data &&
                q->data > root->data)
        {
            root = root->right;
        }
        else
        {
            return root;
        }
    }

    return NULL;
}
```

### Complexity

```text
Average Time: O(log n)

Worst Time: O(n)

Space: O(1)
```

