# 8️⃣ Kth Largest Element in BST

## 📖 Important Idea

Inorder traversal gives:

```text
Ascending Order
```

Reverse inorder gives:

```text
Right → Root → Left
```

which gives:

```text
Descending Order
```

Therefore:

```text
1st visited → Largest

2nd visited → 2nd Largest

3rd visited → 3rd Largest
```

---

### C++ Code

```cpp
void kthLargestHelper(
    Node* root,
    int& k,
    int& answer)
{
    if(root == NULL)
        return;

    kthLargestHelper(
        root->right,
        k,
        answer
    );

    if(k == 0)
        return;

    k--;

    if(k == 0)
    {
        answer = root->data;
        return;
    }

    kthLargestHelper(
        root->left,
        k,
        answer
    );
}

int kthLargest(Node* root, int k)
{
    int answer = -1;

    kthLargestHelper(
        root,
        k,
        answer
    );

    return answer;
}
```

