# 9️⃣ Inorder Successor in BST

## 📖 Definition

The inorder successor of a node is the smallest value greater than that node.

Example:

```text
Inorder:

2 3 4 5 6 7 8
```

Successor of:

```text
5
```

is:

```text
6
```

---

# 🔟 Finding Successor

There are two cases.

### Case 1: Node has a right subtree

The successor is:

```text
Leftmost node of right subtree
```

### Case 2: Node has no right subtree

Move from the root and track the nearest ancestor greater than the target.

---

### C++ Code

```cpp
Node* inorderSuccessor(
    Node* root,
    Node* target)
{
    Node* successor = NULL;

    while(root != NULL)
    {
        if(target->data < root->data)
        {
            successor = root;
            root = root->left;
        }
        else
        {
            root = root->right;
        }
    }

    return successor;
}
```

---

# 1️⃣1️⃣ Inorder Predecessor in BST

## 📖 Definition

The inorder predecessor is the largest value smaller than the given node.

Example:

```text
Inorder:

2 3 4 5 6 7 8
```

Predecessor of:

```text
5
```

is:

```text
4
```

---

### C++ Code

```cpp
Node* inorderPredecessor(
    Node* root,
    Node* target)
{
    Node* predecessor = NULL;

    while(root != NULL)
    {
        if(target->data > root->data)
        {
            predecessor = root;
            root = root->right;
        }
        else
        {
            root = root->left;
        }
    }

    return predecessor;
}
```

