# 💡 Interview Tips

✅ Always use the BST property before choosing a traversal.

✅ For LCA, compare both target values with the current node.

✅ For validation, use a range instead of checking only parent-child relationships.

✅ Reverse inorder is useful for kth largest.

✅ Normal inorder is useful for kth smallest.

✅ Floor and Ceil can be solved efficiently without traversing the entire tree.

---

# ⚠️ Common Mistakes

❌ Checking only whether left child < root and right child > root while validating a BST.

❌ Forgetting the two-child case during deletion.

❌ Confusing predecessor and successor.

❌ Using normal inorder for kth largest instead of reverse inorder.

❌ Forgetting that Floor and Ceil may not exist.

❌ Assuming BST operations are always O(log n).

